"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-19/omp-19/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/2/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/6e66a13a8fa112148a94c97b17706eed8dc1d73b/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates float products (`19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 `1998`). Fix by converting via the decimal representation with explicit half-up rounding.\nFixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py`, in `to_cents`. It did `int(amount * 100)`, which cuts off the decimals instead of rounding. Because floats can't store most decimal prices exactly, `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.999\u2026`, which became 1998 cents. The same thing happened with `0.29` and `4.35`, and the lost cent then carried through into the subtotal, tax and discount math.\n\n**Change:** `to_cents` now turns the amount into a string, converts it to `Decimal` and rounds half-up to whole cents. Going through the string uses the price as written (`19.99`) rather than the float's slightly-off binary value. I added a docstring saying why, so nobody \"simplifies\" it back to the float multiply. `totals.py`, `tax.py` and `discounts.py` already work in integer cents and didn't need changes.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed, and pip refuses to install packages here (the system Python is externally managed). So I imported the test modules and called each test function directly. All 4 tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and the 1 in `tests/test_report.py` passed. I also spot-checked a few inputs: `0.29\u219229`, `4.35\u2192435`, `1.005\u2192101`, `0.1+0.2\u219230`, `-19.99\u2192-1999`, `10\u21921000`. To confirm with the real runner, run `pytest tests` somewhere pytest is installed.\n\n**One thing to know:** an amount with more than two decimal places, such as `1.005`, now rounds half-up to 101 instead of being cut to 100. Exact halves on negative amounts round away from zero. If money ever arrives as strings or `Decimal` rather than floats, `to_cents` handles those too. Passing strings would remove the float problem entirely.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 63933, "requests_cache_write": 31441, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2129476, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 2145, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 2, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T03:24:36.981691+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.591, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2159, "tokens_cache_read": 63933, "tokens_cache_write": 31441, "tokens_fresh": 2159, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 63933, "tokens_main_cache_write": 31441, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 2145, "tokens_output": 2145, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 63933, "tokens_proxy_cache_writ