"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-19/omp-19/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/6e66a13a8fa112148a94c97b17706eed8dc1d73b/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` uses `int(amount * 100)`, which truncates float error (`19.99*100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 1998). Fix by converting through `Decimal` from the decimal string representation.\npytest isn't installed and couldn't be installed, so I'll run the tests directly.\nFixed. The bug was in `to_cents` in `ledger/currency.py`, not in `totals.py`.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` did `int(amount * 100)`. In floating point, `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026`, and `int()` cuts that down to `1998`. So any price whose binary form lands just below the true value lost a cent. That broke `test_subtotal_single` (19.99), `test_subtotal_qty` (0.29) and `test_total_discount` (4.35).\n\n**Fix** (`ledger/currency.py`): `to_cents` now converts the amount to a string first, then to a `Decimal`, multiplies by 100, and rounds half up to a whole cent. Converting via `str` uses the price as written (`\"19.99\"`) instead of its binary approximation. It also rounds properly instead of truncating, so cases like `0.1 + 0.2` correctly give `30`.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here and I couldn't install it, so I imported the test modules and ca